$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Suzuki cross-coupling of 2-bromo-8-methoxyquinoline and binol-bisboronic
acid A mixture of binol-bisboronic acid derivative (1.2 g, 3 mmol),
2-bromo-8-methoxyquinoline1 (2.12 g, 9 mmol, 3 equiv), Pd(PPh3)4 (347 mg,
0.3 mmol, 0.1 equiv), and Ba(OH)2•8 H2O (5.7 g, 18 mmol, 6 equiv), in a
degassed mixture of dioxane (30 mL) and water (10 mL) was heated to 120°C
for 24 h. The reaction mixture was then allowed to cool down to room
temperature and the dioxane was removed using rotary evaporator. The
residue was extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 x 30 mL), washed with 1 N HCl (30
mL), brine solution (30 mL), dried over Na2SO4 and the solvent was
evaporated in vacuo. The crude product was purified by column
chromatography over silica gel. The title tetra-methoxy compound as a
white solid, which was recrystallized from CH2Cl2 and hexane (1.32 g, 70%
yield). IR (neat): ν = 3056, 2936, 2833, 1598, 1258, 1108, 748 cm-1. 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.62 (s, 2H), 8.15 (d, J = 2.8 Hz, 4H), 8.04 (d, J
= 8.0 Hz, 4H), 7.42-7.50 (m, 6H), 7.23-7.28 (m, 4H), 7.13 (d, J = 7.8 Hz,
2H), 4.16 (s, 6H), 3.27 (s, 6H) ppm. 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ 56.2
(2C), 61.5 (2C), 107.8 (2C), 119.5 (2C), 123.8 (2C), 125.2 (2C), 125.8
(2C), 126.0 (2C), 126.7 (2C), 127.0 (2C), 128.5 (2C), 129.1 (2C), 131.2
(2C), 132.8 (2C), 134.1 (2C), 134.6 (2C), 135.8 (2C), 140.6 (2C), 154.2
(2C), 155.8 (2C), 156.3 (2C) ppm. HRMS (ESI): m/z calcd. for C42H32N2O4Na
[M + Na]+, 651.2260; found 651.2259.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Design of a New Bimetallic Catalyst for Asymmetric Epoxidation and
Sulfoxidation
