$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N-(6-(5-Ethoxypyridin-3-yl)benzo[d]thiazol-2-yl)acetamide
2,2,2-trifluoroacetate 6 4 A microwave tube equipped with a magnetic stir
bar was charged with
N-(6-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)benzo[d]thiazol-2-yl)acetamide
27 (60 mg, 0.187 mmol), 3-bromo-5-ethoxypyridine (38.1 mg, 0.187 mmol)
and DMA (2 mL). KOAc (1M, 2 mmol) followed by PdCl2(dppf).CH2Cl2 (7.7 mg,
9.43 umol) were added and the mixture subjected to 10 min of microwave
irradiation at 140 ºC. After cooling, the reaction mixture was diluted
with EtOAc, washed with water and dried over anhydrous Na2SO4. Filtration
and concentration in vacuo gave a residue that was purified by
reverse-phase HPLC using a water/acetonitrile/0.1% trifluoroacetic acid
gradient. Fractions containing pure product were combined and the
volatiles removed in vacuo.
N-(6-(5-ethoxypyridin-3-yl)benzo[d]thiazol-2-yl)acetamide
2,2,2-trifluoroacetate 6 (5.4 mg, 7%) as a white solid. 1H NMR (300 MHz,
DMSO-d 6) δ 12.41 (s, 1H), 8.60 (s, 1H), 8.41 (s, 1H), 8.34-8.30 (m, 1H),
7.84-7.79 (m, 3H), 4.28-4.22 (m, 2H), 2.21(s, 3H), 1.42-1.35 (m, 3H);
ESMS m/z 314.11 (M+ + 1).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Suzuki coupling, product purified by reverse-phase
HPLC and isolated as TFA salt, microwave tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Structural Basis for Isoform Selectivity in a Class of Benzothiazole
Inhibitors of Phosphoinositide 3-Kinase γ
